# RAM

## Goal

Build a parameterized Random Access Memory (RAM) in Verilog that can store, read and write data at different memory addresses.

This project builds on the ROM implementation by adding the ability to modify stored data.

---

# What is RAM?

RAM (Random Access Memory) is a type of memory where data can be both read and written.

The basic operation is:

                 Address
                    │
                    ▼
             ┌─────────────┐
Data In ────►│             │
             │     RAM     │────► Data Out
             │             │
             └──────▲──────┘
                    │
               Write Enable
                    │
                  Clock

The address determines which memory location is accessed.

When "Write Enable" is active, data can be written to that location on the clock edge.

---

# Specifications

| Parameter | Value      |
|-----------|------------|
| Address Width | 4 bits |
| Data Width | 8 bits    |
| Memory Depth | 16      |
| Write | Synchronous    |
| Read | Asynchronous    |

The memory depth is determined by the address width:

2^Address Width = 2^4 = 16

Therefore, the RAM contains 16 memory locations, with each location storing 8 bits.

